    {
      "path": "README.mbt.md",
      "line": 23,
      "kinds": [
        "protocol_capture_audit"
      ],
      "text": "`supersession_fragments` explains prior winners over a correction's valid span, including same-value source changes. `capture_decision` and `audit_decisions` retain facts used by business operations and identify which need recomputation after a late correction. See [Rust bitemporal-runtime comparison](docs/REFERENCE_COMPARISON.md), [complete scenarios](docs/SCENARIOS.md), and [reference provenance](THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md). Evidence is structural JSON without cryptographic signatures; database persistence and business rule execution belong to callers.\r",
      "excerpt_start_column": 1,
      "match_column": 119
    }
